{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1552818-running-the-free-states-10-the-oddball-stuff","id":1552818,"title":"Running the Free States - 10 - The Oddball Stuff","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-08-01T18:03:33-07:00","id":1552818,"title":"Running the Free States - 10 - The Oddball Stuff","content":"This is the tenth and likely the last thread on running a chronicle in the Anarch Free States. I think any comments can probably done or one of the other threads I made. I've covered almost everything I can think of, and my chronicle will likely begin sometime next month. This one is about all the rare clans and bloodlines in VtM and their most likely (or perhaps the most fun) involvement in such a chronicle.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ll start with the Independent clans and what is mentioned. We\u2019ve already covered the Setites on a thread of their own. The other independent clan that gets an official character is the Ravnos. We'll start with them on the next post.<br /> <br /> = = = =<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548164-running-the-free-states-1-the-anarch-council\">Part 1 - the Anarch Council</a>\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548281-running-the-free-states-2-germaine\">Part 2 - Germaine</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548410-running-the-free-states-3-practical-governance\">Part 3 - Governance</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548575-running-the-free-states-4-canon-gangs-npcs\">Part 4 - Canon Characters &amp; Gangs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548935-running-the-free-states-5-setites\">Part 5 - Setites</a><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1549587-running-the-free-states-6-petrodon-and-the-camarilla\">Part 6 - the Camarilla</a>\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550253-running-the-free-states-7-san-francisco-and-the-vampire-club\">Part 7 - San Francisco</a>\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550711-running-the-free-states-8-the-sabbat\">Part 8 - Sabbat</a>\u200b<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551903-running-the-free-states-9-crossover-elements\">Part 9 - Crossovers</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T18:06:00-07:00","id":1552819,"title":"","content":"Ireena is a fairly important character mentioned in LABN, and the first Brujah clanbook mentions a Ravnos representative on the Anarch Council. This points to a noticeable involvement of the Ravnos in the domain, which is a significant departure from any other published city sourcebooks. Not that they don't have any Ravnos characters in them, just that the clan as a whole isn't that important to the domain.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs seem to welcome the Ravnos just like they do a vampire from any other clan. We\u2019re not given any information about them except for Ireena and her \u201cfamily\u201d of a dozen mixed Kindred and kine. Ireena doesn\u2019t appear to be gypsy herself. It\u2019s a name (as Irena) usually associated with the western Slavs, and Ireena herself was an orphaned street kid from Chicago who became a migrant worker who was later embraced by the Ravnos. She\u2019s probably of Polish (or similar) heritage herself. I imagine her mixed group isn\u2019t gypsy either, but made up of similar vagabonds, runaways, and hobos like herself. They are often not in Los Angeles, but travelling elsewhere. It\u2019s probably a good idea for the ST to create such a travelling coterie composed of 4-6 Ravnos (likely all descended from Ireena) and their remaining ghouls and retainers.<br /> <br /> However, I think it would be best to have similar individual Ravnos or coteries of Ravnos that also frequently visit LA. Not enough for the clan to takeover the setting, but enough to demonstrate the Free States are different from other domains by the presence and acceptance of the Ravnos. (This does tend to be one factor that alienates some Gangrel who have their own reasons to be hostile towards the Ravnos.) Are there any obvious candidates from canon sources? We'll take a look at that next.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T10:51:02-07:00","id":1552882,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to pop in and apologise for being an absentee fan: I\u2019m afraid that my ideas dried up a little, so my suggestions have not been flowing in.<br /> <br /> Keep well and please keep up the good work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T16:38:02-07:00","id":1552892,"title":"","content":"One of these other Ravnos in LA will be Alexis Sorokin (Danya) from the Kindred\u2019s Most Wanted (making her the THIRD such vampire on the Red List I am including in the chronicle). I will be placing one of her havens (she has many in vaious cities around the world) in LA because I imagine it\u2019s a good town for one of the world\u2019s best art thieves. She\u2019ll use an alias that she uses just for this town. It\u2019s mentioned she likes to disguise herself as Marilyn Monroe, and this may be how she sometimes (or most often?) appears while in LA. But not all the time, she'll have some other low-key vampire identity as well. I don\u2019t imagine the mystery of her identity will ever come into play by the chronicle, but I like the idea that she sometimes stays in LA and there will be opportunities for the PCs to eventually meet her in some guise. I\u2019ll just have to see how that turns out.<br /> <br /> Another Ravnos who will be mentioned in the Free states is the Spider-killer from the first Ravnos Clanbook. He stalks the cities and deserts of the American Southwest and first appeared in 1894 in Tucson. He\u2019s been seen in California and Mexico. He has attacked both anarchs and elders, but favors targetting the Setites and Mexican Sabbat. A famous story about him is that he discovered a secret Setite community in Phoenix and gave that knowledge to the Prince of Phoenix presumably for free. He appears to be of Native American stock, and one rumor about him is that perhaps he\u2019s not Ravnos at all, but a werecoyote. In actuality, I think he is probably just one of the Wuzho, a 1st edition clanbook concept of Ravnos who dedicate themselves to protecting their clan and destroying their vampire enemies in other clans (also probably heavily influenced by the original Path of Paradox). (I don't think this is mentioned at all in the Revised clanbook which heavily rewrites the entire clan, something Revised did for many clans and bloodlines). I probably won\u2019t have him show up in LA itself, but will name drop him as a danger around the Free States because he\u2019s been known to kill anarchs. When asked about the Spider-killer, the other Ravnos just shrug. He's not a problem for them.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll also include a few other Ravnos of my own creation for flavor purposes. The Ravnos as a clan was something White Wolf really struggled with, and this shows up on these forums as well. I'll use a mix of things from all editions combined with various comments and posts by others here in terms of how I'll portray the clan in general. I\u2019ll probably just review some of the character templates in the clanbook and adopt those I think have the most potential for the chronicle. They\u2019ll just appear every now and again for mostly flavor purposes. But just in case the PCs interact with one or more, I\u2019ll try to make each one interesting enough to justify their interest.<br /> <br /> While Ravnos appreciate the greater freedom and are welcomed by the Free States, many of them still view the Kindred there as marks to be exploited. The Ravnos and Anarchs have certain things in common, but they are not the same and are not aligned. The big difference is that there is likely a greater likelihood of individual Ravnos having real \u201cfriends\u201d among the anarchs (meaning they do not steal from them). However, this only means that they don\u2019t steal from this group of anarchs, instead steal from that other group of anarchs while they\u2019re there. And a different Ravnos will have different friends so... Also, the anarchs being anarchs doesn\u2019t necessarily make them any less of a problem for those Ravnos on the Path of Paradox. Individual Ravnos may adopt the friendship or even the ideology of the anarchs to varying degrees, but most Ravnos simply don\u2019t see themselves as having a stake in the Movement.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-06T12:34:24-07:00","id":1552958,"title":"","content":"The Giovanni get a brief mention in the LABN sourcebook. There don\u2019t seem to be any in the Free States themselves. Instead, the Giovanni observes from Las Vegas. They see the Free States as an unpredictable force that could threaten their clan interests, especially if they come to Las Vegas and \u201cliberate\u201d it. They hope to find an exploitable weakness so their interests cannot be threatened. So per canon, the Giovanni don't really have a presence in LA. That doesn't mean there can't be any Giovanni characters and still keep to canon, but any such characters are probably on the downlow.<br /> <br /> Usually Clan Giovanni is seen as an \u201cally\u201d of the anarchs. That makes sense in Camarilla domains where a Prince is in power, and the Giovanni can gain favors through anarchs and weaken the local status quo powers in order to expand their interests in that domain. However, that scenario does not exist in the Free States. The anarchs are the powers that be. Any Giovanni influence there would come at anarch expense. Giovanni involvement wouldn't be seen as acts of friendship, but as intervention by interlopers.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-06T12:42:23-07:00","id":1552959,"title":"","content":"Furthermore, the anarchs shouldn\u2019t like the internal dynamics of Clan Giovanni. It is a clan ruled absolutely by its third generation founder. Every Giovanni is supposed to obey bottom up in a strict hierarchy. If this was a clan of the Camarilla, it\u2019d be seen as more oppressive than the Tremere or Ventrue. Anarchs can have a tactical alliance with the Giovanni in many domains, but the Movement itself can never be strategically allied to the Giovanni. That clan represents some of the worse of elder tyranny.<br /> <br /> There is even the issue of younger Giovanni - perhaps angry at being told what to do - wanting to \u201cgo anarch\u201d themselves and free themselves from the rule of Augustus Giovanni. After all, if you were born in the late twentieth century, what real loyalty might you have to some undead fossil from the Early Middle Ages? Especially if you are from one of the other families and not identify as being from the mortal Giovanni family (even if there is some intermarriage)? There should be some Giovanni - despite their supposed double loyalty from both clan and family ties - who may want to get out from under the thumb of their clan elders. Most anarchs would be sympathetic to that and thus see the Giovanni elders as enemies just as they do for the other clans.<br /> <br /> The last thing the Giovanni would want is for an ideology that encourages their younger members to wage war against the elders. This might not happen in a typical Camarilla domain, but the Free States and the ideology of the Movement represents a real danger to the Giovanni that individual anarchs like a Juggler, Hinds, or Dickie Fulcher does not.<br /> <br /> Now whether or not any Giovanni neonates (or others) could successfully possibly defect to the anarchs is debatable. You would have to make a judgment based on your assumptions about the clan size, the success of clan grooming/brainwashing/indoctrination over its neonates, active oversight of Augustus, the effectiveness or Necromancy to spy and attack and countermeasures to that, plus other things. Nevertheless, I don't think the Giovanni consider themselves immune to anarch sympathies, so they would need to battle it lest it become a problem.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-06T12:46:43-07:00","id":1552960,"title":"","content":"So I am putting down Clan Giovanni as an enemy to the Free States as seen by the leaders and malcontents of the Free States themselves. Not as serious as the Camarilla or Setites, but someone they don\u2019t want to tolerate in southern California. Furthermore, they also understand that any attempt to liberate Las Vegas would cause the local Giovanni there to side against them.<br /> <br /> So I won\u2019t be including any typical Giovanni in the chronicle. I am on the fence whether to have some Giovanni vampire there who is hiding out from the clan due to her crimes and therefore would be destroyed, tortured, or blood bonded if ever found out or caught. Such a Giovanni won't advertise as Giovanni though. Better for everyone to just think they are Brujah, Caitiff, or any other clan.<br /> <br /> However, I am also thinking about including either one or two surviving Cappadocians in LA (if two, it\u2019d be a sire and her childe). These would be \u201cmodern\u201d Cappadocians descended from those who survived the purge. While the first three editions liked to play up the idea that the Cappadocians were all destroyed by the mighty Giovanni, that was already suspect even in second edition. In the era of V5 where the Giovanni are simply one part of a greater Hecata clan, I think it makes even less sense to pretend the Giovanni were ever successful at wiping out all the Cappadocians. This is something that would seem out of place if I ran this chronicle back in 1994 and bring protest by players as being too special or cheesy, but I don\u2019t think it would be much controversial now in 2025. (Of course, they too would likely never advertise their true clan. You don't want that attention to yourself)<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a treatment I\u2019ll be use again in this thread. Los Angeles would be very attractive for a whole lot of \u201chunted\u201d vampires because the traditional power structure is broken down. It\u2019s a huge domain whose population is not well tracked. It\u2019s a great place to hide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-08T12:44:22-07:00","id":1553014,"title":"","content":"The Assamites get even less mentioned. They were contracted by the Inner Circle to destroy Jeremy MacNeil in 1955. They failed, and per their rules, MacNeil is now off limits to them. They may still accept contracts on other anarchs in the Free States. I think that is it for the LABN sourcebook.<br /> <br /> The only other possible Assamite reference to the Free States that I can think of is in the description of Badr-al-Budur in Milwaukee By Night. Although her home base is Milwaukee, she travels across the Northwest. Her \u201calliance with the Anarchs\u201d gives her blood across the continent while elders from Chicago to San Francisco hire her for their needs. To me, this sounds like Badr has some kind of geographic remit from west of the Great Lakes to the West Coast. That might include the Free States (albeit southen California is clearly not \u201cthe Northwest\u201d). She works for anyone of course.<br /> <br /> Does &quot;alliance with the Anarchs&quot; indicate ties to the Free States? Or just local anarchs? If it is just connections to local anarchs, why would it be called an &quot;alliance&quot; when so many Camarilla elders also use her? If Badr takes contracts from the anarchs in LA, she is likely not the Assamite used to fulfil contracts <i>against</i> LA anarchs. Those would be other Assamites hired elsewhere. However, it might be interesting to include Badr if an NPC or PC reaches out to the Assamites for an assassination.<br /> <br /> But is that all? Given the chaos and violence of the Free States, could the Assamites make some use of it? We\u2019re told that Assamites have exceptionally long apprenticeships where they learn how to do things even as newly embraced neonates. Could there be a cell of such Assamites in LA utilizing it as a useful training ground? Or is that just too fanciful, obvious, lame, or come with too many drawbacks compared to its benefits? The Free States is probably already home to a lot of unusual Kindred so this may be too much.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-11T11:34:14-07:00","id":1553071,"title":"","content":"Past the Independent Clans, there are still a variety of bloodlines and small sects of vampires in the VtM setting. Normally I NEVER include them in chronicles I run. I feel unless you intend to do something special concerning them, it is just best not to use them. Otherwise you run the risk of making those elements seem less rare than what they should be. However, I think there\u2019s some compelling reasons to include specific ones in LA. Instead of addressing them one by one, I\u2019ll just mention those I feel have a reason to be there.<br /> <br /> First, I am considering including my first Salubri in a chronicle at all. I\u2019m talking about the original description of the Salubri found in the original Player Guides, not all the stuff added to them since Revised. The remaining seven Salubri (and their childer being trained before they diablerize them) are split up and hidden all over the world. But I think the Free States would be an excellent place for <i>one</i> of them (plus one childe still being trained). It\u2019s a place where the Tremere have no power or representation. The anarchs either won\u2019t believe or don\u2019t care about the rumors the Tremere (and therefore the Camarilla) spread about them. Of course, the Salubri there won\u2019t ever admit to being Salubri and will keep a low profile, but he\u2019ll be there.<br /> <br /> Second, I think the Children of Osiris will have a representative of some kind (again, never admitting who she is). They know the Setites consider LA to be a priority target, and the chaos of the Free States risk the Setites taking over. Having an agent there who can observe things, identify Setite activity, and then take action at some point (probably by manipulating the anarchs to deal with it) makes sense. Assuming the PCs take actions against the Setites at some point, I see this as being the character must likely to come into actual gameplay.<br /> <br /> Third, should there be one of the True Brujah there? LA would be one of the big centers for Brujah power. If the True Brujah want revenge, having someone here observe things would seem to be a good idea. It doesn\u2019t need to be someone who is also in the True Black Hand. Nor does the vampire need to always be in LA proper. She can have an local estate elsewhere and simply visit from time to time, using an alternate identity crafted just for this. Mostly just observing, but sometimes doing something to thwart the plans of the Brujah (in a way that won\u2019t expose her identity or bring risk). While I normally stay clear of including ANY bloodlines in a chronicle, I would double that for True Brujah (mostly because of the backlash against Temporis as the &quot;time travel Discipline&quot;. Yet if the bloodline exists and is observing the Brujah in the hope of thwarting that clan, wouldn\u2019t the Free States be a place you\u2019d want one of you to be? Tell me what you think.<br /> <br /> Those are the ones most apparent to me. Naturally they\u2019ll be claiming to be some other clan of vampire and try to limit their exposure while not being so reclusive as to generate suspicion. Determining a good cover identity for each of them will probably take more time than their core concept itself.<br /> <br /> Since I don\u2019t plan on running any active plots with them, they will be sandbox elements the PCs may or may not stumble across. I\u2019d like to find something interesting for a True Brujah character to do (even if never revealing the character to be True Brujah) simply because the Free States are so dominated by Brujah that it would make sense for some machinations to be going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T05:41:04-08:00","id":1555845,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, it struck me recently that it has been some little while since there was a new entry on this thread, so I wanted to confirm if that\u2019s because you\u2019ve started running the campaign - is this in fact the case?<br /> <br /> If so, I hope that things have been going well for all and that you\u2019ve had fun playing all the dominos set in place on these diverse threads.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T10:06:40-08:00","id":1555856,"title":"","content":"The chronicle should begin in January after the holidays. The players have created their PCs, and we've done some brief preludes. I'm spending most of my time determining the concrete details for those aspects of the chronicle the PCs will likely encounter first. Some of things discussed on the threads may be more theoretical than implemented into play. I'll have to see how things go. However, the brainstorming was very helpful even if ultimately I don't do anything with certain ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T14:08:51-08:00","id":1555923,"title":"","content":"I look forward to seeing what proved useful, whenever you\u2019re able to share the \u2018sizzle reel\u2019 from your campaign, assuming you be willing.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}